# The words of the standard settings, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
setting-label-fs-shell-language = Language
setting-about-fs-shell-language = The language of the program's words.
setting-label-fs-look-style = Style
setting-about-fs-look-style = The look of the program (its style).
setting-label-fs-look-scheme = Light or dark
setting-about-fs-look-scheme = Light or dark colours; without a choice the system decides.
setting-label-fs-shell-frontend = Program frontend
setting-about-fs-shell-frontend = The frontend the program opens. Without a choice the program's own default is used.
setting-label-fs-shell-refresh-ms = Check for changes every (ms)
setting-about-fs-shell-refresh-ms = How often the program looks for changed settings while a window is open.
setting-error-reason-missing = Locking {$key} needs a reason.
